Upstream licence exceptions
---------------------------
mautrix-meta and mautrix-linkedin both ship LICENSE.exceptions granting:
- Beeper: right to embed in Beeper clients/servers and distribute the
  collective work without applying the AGPL to the whole;
- Element: right to distribute compiled binaries in server bundles.
Both conditional on modifications to the mautrix code staying public under
AGPL v3+. These exceptions are named grants. They do NOT apply to MINI.

Distribution rule (in force until a licensing decision is recorded)
-------------------------------------------------------------------
- Builds containing libgojni.so are private developer builds. Do not share
  them with anyone, including testers.
- The release variant must not contain the runtime. build.gradle.kts fails
  release tasks if it does, unless -Pmini.licenseDecision is set to a
  recorded decision.
- Before any distribution: choose AGPL-for-MINI and/or obtain upstream
  exceptions (mautrix and libsignal), add in-app Appropriate Legal Notices,
  publish Corresponding Source for the exact build, and include all
  third-party notices. See the checklist in the compliance doc.
- Never patch upstream sources in place. Use a public fork with dated change
  notes and a go.mod replace.
